28	// stdin and answers each independently — `<sha> commit <size>` for one that resolves,
29	// `<input> missing` for one that does not — so it is the same revision parser
30	// `rev-parse --verify` uses, `^{commit}` peeling included, asked four questions at
31	// once instead of four times. A repo whose base is a local `main` (every check fixture,
32	// and any clone without a remote) missed on both `origin/` candidates first and paid
33	// three spawns for an answer that now costs one.
